man-Write-Error = writes an error (a non-terminating one: what follows still runs), in PowerShell's layout; it goes into $Error.
    .synopsis = Write-Error [-Message] <String>
    .option-Message = the error's text.
    .example-1 = an error of your own
man-Get-Member = shows what an object is made of: its type (TypeName) and its members, properties and methods. The first reflex in front of an unknown object: Get-Service | Get-Member.
    .synopsis = Get-Member [[-Name] <String[]>] [-MemberType <PSMemberTypes>]
